# E345 draft - zero-dependency meson library pattern for OHOS Conan

id:                     E345
trigger_tool:           meson|ninja
phase:                  configuration|compilation
error_signature:        Dependency .* not found|Library m found: NO|shared_library.*cannot be linked|C compiler cannot create executables

severity:               2
category:               ohos, meson, conan, relocatable, zero-dependency
match_keywords:         MesonToolchain, cc.find_library, libm, bionic, shared_library version, llvm-ar, llvm-ranlib, binary-sign-tool, TMPDIR
title:                  Adapt a zero-dependency Meson C library to OHOS with a shared-only toolchain, LLVM archive tools, and ELF signing

root_cause:             A Meson library that declares no pkg-config dependencies still needs four OHOS-specific fixes: (1) the SDK profile often only names clang, so Meson cannot find ar/ranlib for the native file and fails the static or shared archive step; (2) the OHOS worker has no usable /tmp, so clang and ninja fail creating temporary files unless TMPDIR points inside the build folder; (3) math functions live in bionic libc, so the upstream optional cc.find_library('m', required:false) must not abort configure; (4) shared libraries installed by Meson are unsigned ELF and refuse to load on the device until binary-sign-tool stamps a .codesign section.
affected_scope:         Small C libraries whose upstream Meson build only links optional system libs (e.g. libxcvt 0.1.3, which generates VESA CVT modelines) and that are packaged as shared libraries on an aarch64 OHOS worker.
verification_cmd:       Run a single-package shadow CI build; require meson setup + ninja to finish, test_package to compile and run the consumer, and readelf -SW on the packaged libxcvt.so.0.1.3 to confirm exactly one .codesign section.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           shared-only-meson-toolchain-with-llvm-tools
rec_description:        Build with MesonToolchain and default_library=shared, inject llvm-ar/ranlib full paths into conan_meson_native.ini when the profile only declares clang, pin TMPDIR/TMP/TEMP into the build folder, install meson via pip when absent, and ELF-sign every packaged .so (and bin/) with llvm-objcopy --remove-section .codesign then binary-sign-tool sign -selfSign 1.
rec_command:            CI_PACKAGES="archives/l/libxcvt/0.1.3" zsh ci/conan/build_and_test.sh
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      system-tool-path-probing
fallback_description:   When llvm-ar is not co-located with clang, resolve ar/ranlib through PATH (llvm-ar, ar, llvm-ranlib, ranlib) and write them into the Meson native file; if even PATH lacks them, fall back to the SDK tool dirs the profile exposes.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          conan-recipe

forbid_1_pattern:       strip.*\.codesign|sign.*\.so.*without.*objcopy
forbid_1_reason:        Re-signing without first removing the previous .codesign section leaves duplicate sections and an invalid signature that can still fail on device.
forbid_1_consequence:   The signed .so loads in the sandbox but is rejected on real hardware.
forbid_2_pattern:       hardcode.*/tmp|mktemp.*/tmp
forbid_2_reason:        The OHOS worker has no writable /tmp; a hard-coded /tmp TMPDIR fails for clang temp files.
forbid_2_consequence:   C compiler cannot create executables, even when the toolchain itself is healthy.

principles:             P013,P014
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             E337
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

